1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:03,565
Before anyone yells "action"...

2
00:00:03,595 --> 00:00:05,135
who is this video for?

3
00:00:05,438 --> 00:00:06,723
A beautiful film,

4
00:00:06,753 --> 00:00:08,563
made for the wrong audience,

5
00:00:08,658 --> 00:00:10,466
plays to an empty room.

6
00:00:10,789 --> 00:00:12,829
And no edit, no grade,

7
00:00:12,859 --> 00:00:14,614
no soundtrack can fix

8
00:00:14,644 --> 00:00:16,029
the wrong message.

9
00:00:16,191 --> 00:00:17,821
Your audience is already

10
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,456
leaving footprints.

11
00:00:19,486 --> 00:00:20,711
What they search.

12
00:00:20,741 --> 00:00:23,711
Save. Skip. Share.

13
00:00:23,741 --> 00:00:25,099
Follow them first.

14
00:00:25,263 --> 00:00:27,333
Research tells you who to cast,

15
00:00:27,363 --> 00:00:28,123
what hooks them

16
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:29,338
in three seconds,

17
00:00:29,368 --> 00:00:31,083
and whether to shoot vertical...

18
00:00:31,113 --> 00:00:31,964
or wide.

19
00:00:32,201 --> 00:00:33,551
Change it on paper?

20
00:00:33,581 --> 00:00:35,606
That costs an afternoon.

21
00:00:35,636 --> 00:00:37,396
Change it after the shoot?

22
00:00:37,426 --> 00:00:38,781
That's a reshoot.

23
00:00:38,811 --> 00:00:40,224
Research first.

24
00:00:40,281 --> 00:00:40,906
Then roll.

25
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:44,071
Esha Bargate Productions.

26
00:00:44,101 --> 00:00:45,796
Let's find your audience...

27
00:00:45,951 --> 00:00:47,990
before we frame a single shot.

